{"chunk_id": "7840b049ba11", "text": "This section recounts the dramatic aftermath of Arjuna\u2019s vow to slay Jayadratha. Arjuna releases a mantra-charged arrow that severs Jayadratha\u2019s head and miraculously carries it through the sky to fall onto the lap of his father, Vriddhakshatra; when the king rises, the head drops and the curse causes his own skull to shatter. Krishna then dispels the illusory darkness that had enabled Arjuna to fulfill his vow. As the battle resumes, Arjuna refuses to kill his elders Kripa and Ashwatthaman, fighting them with restrained force and later lamenting that he has wounded his own preceptor. Meanwhile Karna charges forward, prompting a spectacular duel between Karna and Satyaki. With Krishna\u2019s chariot supplied by Daruka, Satyaki fights brilliantly, destroys Karna\u2019s chariot, and throws the Kaurava army into dismay, while vows and rivalries continue to shape who may kill whom.\nArjuna kills Jayadratha through Krishna\u2019s stratagem; he spares Kripa in remorse while Satyaki duels Karna and temporarily makes him carless.\nThemes: fulfilled vow, divine stratagem, guru reverence and remorse, heroic duels, warrior vows", "vector": [0.012574635446071625, -0.005441675428301096, -0.005871371831744909, 0.017394110560417175, -0.0076039074920117855, 0.01843913272023201, -0.0040838345885276794, -0.004544469062238932, -0.02374674193561077, -0.011935247108340263, 0.017064103856682777, 0.013434028252959251, -0.004626970738172531, 0.008786432445049286, 0.00686139240860939, 0.0007652892963960767, 0.040508341044187546, -0.015317817218601704, 0.03407320752739906, -0.02524552308022976, 0.0018236315809190273, 0.012402757070958614, 0.00476791150867939, 0.030470632016658783, -0.005510426592081785, 0.03036062978208065, -0.013915288262069225, -0.025094270706176758, 0.024544259533286095, -0.0046819718554615974, -0.013489029370248318, -0.0017153481021523476, 0.0037744531873613596, -0.009515197016298771, -0.035448234528303146, 0.02750056982040